  "responsibility_boundary": "Wave 7 separates Skill CLI authoring, lifecycle, and runtime presentation while retaining the Wave 4 storage, Wave 5 Agent CLI, and Wave 6 Work Lab owners behind stable public facades.",
  "cohesion_rationale": "The four Skill CLI owners are the minimum cohesive split for independently changing authoring, lifecycle, runtime, and shared command seams; the exact scope also renews the eleven still-live owner files from Waves 4 through 6 required by the owner-wide issue root.",
  "rejected_split_alternatives": [
    "Folding Skill authoring, lifecycle, or runtime commands back into skill.py would restore the mixed-responsibility module this wave removes.",
    "Combining Skill CLI helpers with storage, Agent CLI, or Work Lab owners would couple unrelated persistence, execution, and presentation responsibilities.",
    "Relabeling handwritten files or changing stable command callbacks would hide responsibility or break supported imports instead of reducing complexity."
  ],
